WEBVTT

00:12.519 --> 00:14.521
I'm gonna go get a drink.

00:14.604 --> 00:16.857
Amamiya. I'm coming too.

00:24.531 --> 00:25.991
<i>Without exchanging a word...</i>

00:26.533 --> 00:28.034
<i>We've arrived.</i>

00:38.837 --> 00:45.343
Hey, do you think they'll be surprised
if they come back to find nobody here?

00:45.427 --> 00:46.887
Shall we?

00:46.970 --> 00:48.346
THESE TWO HAVE
COMPLETELY GONE OFF TRACK

00:50.557 --> 00:51.892
- <i>So cold...</i>
- <i>So hot...</i>

00:51.975 --> 00:52.976
THUMP THUMP

00:53.059 --> 00:54.102
Minato!

00:55.937 --> 00:57.230
Kenta. Hello.

00:57.731 --> 00:59.733
You doing those questions I gave you?

01:01.193 --> 01:02.402
<i>Seniors.</i>

01:03.070 --> 01:05.739
- <i>Scurry, scurry.</i>
- I was doing them till just a second ago.

01:05.822 --> 01:07.115
You sure about that?

01:08.867 --> 01:10.035
Is this one of your juniors?

01:10.118 --> 01:11.578
Yep. Cutie, isn't he?

01:11.661 --> 01:13.830
Does Kenta look out for you
like he should?

01:13.914 --> 01:16.875
He loves to pretend he's all that,
but he couldn't be farther from "that."

01:16.958 --> 01:18.418
I beg your pardon?

01:18.502 --> 01:20.253
FADE

01:20.337 --> 01:21.797
- See ya.
- Bye-bye.

01:21.880 --> 01:22.881
See you.

01:23.715 --> 01:24.716
POKE OUT

01:24.800 --> 01:26.635
- Are you done?
- Hikawa?

01:27.469 --> 01:30.096
You could have
just been yourself, you know.

01:30.597 --> 01:31.848
It's not that.

01:32.432 --> 01:33.934
It's not that I wasn't being myself,

01:34.017 --> 01:35.936
it's just that I don't know
those older people.

01:36.937 --> 01:38.188
Were you scared?

01:38.271 --> 01:39.564
MEMORIES OF MIDDLE SCHOOL

01:39.648 --> 01:40.649
A little.

01:40.732 --> 01:42.400
<i>So she's shy around strangers...</i>

01:48.365 --> 01:49.699
Hikawa.

01:51.201 --> 01:54.287
Are you maybe scared of me too?

01:54.371 --> 01:55.372
Huh?

01:57.749 --> 01:58.959
No.

01:59.042 --> 02:00.168
<i>Not anymore.</i>

02:00.669 --> 02:02.045
I'm not scared of you.

02:08.844 --> 02:10.554
Thank goodness.

02:15.267 --> 02:18.687
<i>Of course. Amamiya is human too.</i>

02:18.770 --> 02:21.273
<i>He hurts, and worries over things too.</i>

02:21.898 --> 02:24.151
<i>This is all so obvious, and yet...</i>

02:25.277 --> 02:28.780
<i>Just how have I been treating him
all this time?</i>

02:31.783 --> 02:33.201
Amamiya.

02:33.785 --> 02:36.454
<i>Man, what do I do?
I can't look her in the face.</i>

02:39.791 --> 02:40.792
Huh?

02:44.004 --> 02:45.922
- A co-co-co--
- Co?

02:46.006 --> 02:48.091
There! Down there! Behind you!

02:48.175 --> 02:50.635
Look! There! There!

02:50.719 --> 02:52.262
Huh? What?

03:00.020 --> 03:01.771
HEH - HAH

03:03.857 --> 03:05.066
Oh, my gosh...

03:06.985 --> 03:08.528
I thought you'd gone mad!

03:08.612 --> 03:11.531
Well, because... Sorry about that.

03:12.908 --> 03:16.036
<i>I don't want to be friends
by me prying open the door.</i>

03:16.870 --> 03:18.788
<i>I want to know you for you.</i>

03:18.872 --> 03:20.290
<i>I want to be genuine friends.</i>

03:20.874 --> 03:22.125
<i>I want you to smile.</i>

03:22.918 --> 03:24.210
<i>That's all.</i>

03:26.129 --> 03:27.547
<i>That's all it was.</i>

03:28.423 --> 03:29.841
<i>And yet...</i>

05:01.558 --> 05:05.979
EPISODE 9
SELF-AWARENESS

05:06.813 --> 05:08.481
They sure are taking their time.

05:10.817 --> 05:12.652
Isn't this way too long
for a little break?

05:12.736 --> 05:14.279
Do they even want to study?

05:14.362 --> 05:15.655
Exams are coming up, you know.

05:15.739 --> 05:18.033
- You're one to talk.
- Says you!

05:18.116 --> 05:20.160
OPERATION "SURPRISE THEM
WHEN THEY COME BACK"

05:21.786 --> 05:23.163
So, Yota.

05:23.830 --> 05:25.081
Who do you like?

05:26.750 --> 05:28.251
Why do you ask?

05:28.335 --> 05:33.173
Well, you never talk about this stuff.
So I'm curious.

05:38.803 --> 05:39.804
Miki.

05:39.888 --> 05:40.889
Huh?

05:46.853 --> 05:48.938
- Koyun.
- Huh?

05:49.022 --> 05:51.691
Hayato, Daichi, Gin.

05:51.775 --> 05:54.611
Mom, Dad, Haruto, Sakura.

05:54.694 --> 05:56.279
Whoa, slow down there.

05:56.362 --> 05:57.947
At least include Minato, please.

06:02.118 --> 06:03.703
Hey, Yota.

06:03.787 --> 06:09.042
If you ever do get a crush on someone,
I'll be right there to have your back.

06:09.542 --> 06:12.337
Seeing as you've done so much for me.

06:17.842 --> 06:20.220
- I knew I could count on you.
- Yeah!

06:21.805 --> 06:23.306
Hey, they're back.

06:24.808 --> 06:26.518
Huh? Where is everyone?

06:26.601 --> 06:29.145
All their stuff is still here.
Maybe they went to the bathroom?

06:31.564 --> 06:33.733
Well, wherever it is,
they'll be back soon.

06:34.234 --> 06:35.235
I guess you're right.

06:38.363 --> 06:43.493
<i>The way Yota suppresses his feelings
in order to stay friends with Miki...</i>

06:44.160 --> 06:46.246
<i>I can tell it's draining him.</i>

06:47.080 --> 06:51.251
<i>And similarly, if Hikawa falls for Yota,</i>

06:51.751 --> 06:54.003
<i>he won't return the feelings.</i>

06:54.838 --> 06:56.506
<i>She really shouldn't go there...</i>

06:57.298 --> 06:59.008
<i>Or so I thought.</i>

07:00.009 --> 07:04.347
<i>But really, these aren't the things that
you can just will in and out of existence.</i>

07:07.725 --> 07:09.519
<i>I wish I hadn't noticed this.</i>

07:10.603 --> 07:13.815
<i>It feels like she's finally
opened up a little to me.</i>

07:14.607 --> 07:17.402
- <i>So I can't just barge in and--</i>
- Amamiya.

07:21.156 --> 07:22.282
Here.

07:22.365 --> 07:24.868
I've only got two left.
So take it while you can.

07:29.164 --> 07:30.415
Thank you.

07:33.042 --> 07:34.169
<i>This sucks...</i>

07:34.252 --> 07:35.253
POPPING OUT

07:35.336 --> 07:37.505
- "Take it while you can?" Ouch!
- You were here?

07:43.219 --> 07:44.220
ART ROOM

07:44.304 --> 07:46.764
Have you always had lunch here
in the Art Room, Tsukiko?

07:46.848 --> 07:51.144
Yeah. I can finish my lunch early here
and then get straight back to work.

07:52.896 --> 07:54.272
Very practical.

07:54.355 --> 07:56.357
APPEARED IN EP 6
GRADE 1 CLASS 2 - LIBRARY REP

07:56.441 --> 07:57.775
I'm Tsukiko Shimojima.

07:58.443 --> 08:02.530
I did start out eating
with everyone in the classroom.

08:02.614 --> 08:05.867
<i>But we had a pretty big group, and
it's not like we were all best buddies.</i>

08:05.950 --> 08:07.660
GROUP THAT JUST CAME TO BE
SAME MIDDLE SCHOOL - FRIENDS

08:07.744 --> 08:09.037
SAME CLUB - SIT TOGETHER
ALWAYS CHATTING

08:09.120 --> 08:15.793
<i>We also had this unspoken rule that we all
had to wait for everyone before we'd eat.</i>

08:15.877 --> 08:20.298
I thought to myself, "Wait,
is this really what close friends do?"

08:20.381 --> 08:24.302
So I started distancing myself,
and kind of broke away from the group.

08:24.385 --> 08:25.803
HAHA

08:27.639 --> 08:30.850
But it's not that I left
on bad terms or anything.

08:30.934 --> 08:33.019
I still hang out with everyone separately.

08:33.520 --> 08:37.148
<i>Oh, no! Now she's going
to think I'm a terrible person.</i>

08:37.232 --> 08:38.566
I get it.

08:39.150 --> 08:41.819
I get it so much that now I feel sick.

08:41.903 --> 08:43.488
<i>Empathy.</i>

08:43.571 --> 08:45.240
Are you okay?

08:45.740 --> 08:49.077
Well, I'm not very good
at operating in groups either.

08:49.577 --> 08:51.829
<i>Honestly, I can see it.</i>

08:51.913 --> 08:54.082
LOOKING

08:56.167 --> 08:57.335
Oh, man.

08:57.418 --> 09:00.838
If only we'd been able to chat sooner.

09:02.924 --> 09:04.050
YAY

09:04.133 --> 09:05.468
Strawberries today.

09:05.552 --> 09:06.928
Would you like some?

09:07.011 --> 09:08.346
Are you sure?

09:08.429 --> 09:11.349
GRADE 1 CLASS 6

09:11.432 --> 09:13.059
AFTER SCHOOL STUDY SESSION

09:13.142 --> 09:14.852
So, curry...

09:15.937 --> 09:17.105
Anyone want curry?

09:17.188 --> 09:18.606
- Huh?
- What?

09:18.690 --> 09:21.484
I mean, when do we ever not want curry?

09:21.568 --> 09:23.611
You're on board! I like you.

09:24.404 --> 09:28.116
So, there's apparently this famous curry
place at the new mall that just opened up.

09:28.199 --> 09:29.325
MAKE A LITTLE PIT STOP

09:29.409 --> 09:30.535
- Can we go?
- Sure.

09:30.618 --> 09:31.911
COVERED BY THEIR COMMUTER PASS

09:31.995 --> 09:34.289
But it'll mean you two will have
to ride the train with us.

09:34.372 --> 09:35.415
I don't mind.

09:35.498 --> 09:36.499
Me neither.

09:36.583 --> 09:38.418
What about dinner at home?

09:38.501 --> 09:42.046
Koyun. You're always
worrying about that. I'll be fine.

09:42.130 --> 09:43.131
"Always"?

09:43.214 --> 09:47.135
All right! Then we're having an outing!

09:47.218 --> 09:49.637
STATION - SCHOOL
TROT TROT TROT

09:50.555 --> 09:51.639
Wow.

09:51.723 --> 09:54.934
- Is that where you hold on?
- Yes?

09:55.018 --> 09:56.060
- So jealous.
- Jealous?

09:56.144 --> 09:57.145
SPARKLE SPARKLE

09:57.729 --> 09:59.772
I don't need to hold onto anything.
I can stand.

10:00.273 --> 10:01.316
<i>Core! Strength!</i>

10:01.399 --> 10:02.984
So, that's how you're competing?

10:06.070 --> 10:07.113
You're heavy.

10:07.196 --> 10:08.656
That's not holding your own.

10:08.740 --> 10:10.658
I'm not using my hands,
so it still counts.

10:10.742 --> 10:12.160
No way does that count.

10:25.798 --> 10:29.802
<i>Things have changed so much
from how they were not too long ago.</i>

10:33.056 --> 10:38.895
<i>Middle school felt like a fish tank,
and me a creature that couldn't breathe.</i>

10:39.896 --> 10:42.815
<i>I couldn't be like the others,
and that pained me.</i>

10:43.816 --> 10:46.152
<i>I realized I was living
somewhere where I didn't belong.</i>

10:47.195 --> 10:50.156
<i>But even when I fled,
there was no place to belong.</i>

10:50.740 --> 10:53.534
<i>I felt like I was at fault
for not being able to adapt.</i>

10:54.327 --> 10:56.746
<i>It hurt... It hurt so much...</i>

10:57.830 --> 10:58.831
<i>But then...</i>

11:00.500 --> 11:02.919
<i>Then I found my way out of the fish tank</i>

11:03.836 --> 11:07.340
<i>and I realized I didn't have to endure
the pain of living in a small world.</i>

11:07.423 --> 11:10.593
<i>Once I realized I didn't have to settle,</i>

11:12.011 --> 11:14.430
<i>it all seemed so trivial.</i>

11:17.517 --> 11:18.518
STUDENT COUNCIL NEWSLETTER

11:18.601 --> 11:20.019
DEAR STUDENTS, CONGRATULATIONS
ON ENTERING HIGH SCHOOL

11:20.103 --> 11:21.938
<i>Club activities,
school events, even friends...</i>

11:22.021 --> 11:24.440
<i>If I could just spend
the next three years in peace,</i>

11:25.066 --> 11:26.859
<i>then none of that even matters.</i>

11:31.322 --> 11:33.533
<i>Things have changed a lot since then.</i>

11:34.534 --> 11:38.079
Wow, it's so nice here
around the train station now.

11:39.080 --> 11:41.499
<i>Or maybe I've changed as well?</i>

11:42.417 --> 11:45.128
It's so different
compared to before the mall was here.

11:45.211 --> 11:47.338
I'll bet the rent around here
has gone bonkers.

11:47.422 --> 11:48.631
Who are you to judge?

11:49.132 --> 11:51.175
<i>Yeah. Everything will be fine.</i>

11:52.176 --> 11:56.013
<i>I can just pretend
those bad memories don't exist.</i>

11:56.681 --> 12:00.601
GRAND OPENING SALE

12:01.727 --> 12:06.023
Let's see. We're here,
and the food court is here, so...

12:06.107 --> 12:07.108
FOOD COURT

12:07.191 --> 12:08.192
This way.

12:08.276 --> 12:09.485
POWER WALKING - GAH

12:09.569 --> 12:12.530
I knew you'd come to that conclusion.
It's the opposite direction.

12:12.613 --> 12:13.614
JEEZ

12:13.698 --> 12:15.408
Here. It's this way.

12:15.491 --> 12:17.577
Are you sure?
You're not tricking me, are you?

12:17.660 --> 12:19.120
I'm sure.

12:19.203 --> 12:21.706
<i>Hey, what was that "I know you"
attitude just now?</i>

12:21.789 --> 12:22.790
<i>I can get behind this!</i>

12:22.874 --> 12:23.875
FLASH
POWERED BY FAN LOVE

12:30.131 --> 12:31.215
Really?

12:34.469 --> 12:35.761
Whoa...

12:36.471 --> 12:38.806
- Miki.
- Whoa! Personal space, dude! What is it?

12:38.890 --> 12:41.267
- Igarashi's here.
- What?

12:42.310 --> 12:44.353
We don't get along anymore.

12:44.937 --> 12:47.356
We should keep him away from Hikawa, yeah?

12:49.692 --> 12:51.277
So, Koyun told you?

12:51.777 --> 12:53.362
<i>That they used to date.</i>

12:53.446 --> 12:55.781
Yeah. Very briefly though.

12:56.282 --> 12:57.867
<i>That they're on bad terms.</i>

12:58.451 --> 13:01.329
Do you think it'll turn into a fight
if they do run into each other?

13:01.412 --> 13:04.165
No, I don't think it'd go that far.

13:04.248 --> 13:07.376
Well, either way,
I don't want Hikawa feeling bad.

13:07.460 --> 13:08.628
Let's keep them apart.

13:09.212 --> 13:10.421
Agreed.

13:16.552 --> 13:17.845
What's up, Koyun?

13:18.679 --> 13:19.764
<i>Can't let him see.</i>

13:20.264 --> 13:21.891
- Yota, look! A dog.
- What?

13:21.974 --> 13:23.309
Let's go see it.

13:23.392 --> 13:26.103
But then, maybe nothing will happen.

13:26.187 --> 13:29.398
He could have actually moved on already.

13:29.482 --> 13:31.901
Yeah, I guess you're right.

13:32.527 --> 13:34.153
Hikawa?

13:34.237 --> 13:37.031
I don't remember anyone
by that name from middle school.

13:39.617 --> 13:43.162
<i>Still, to have supposedly forgotten
she even existed...</i>

13:43.746 --> 13:48.209
Well, I guess all we can do is hope
that he gets on with his next girlfriend.

13:48.793 --> 13:50.169
What?

13:50.253 --> 13:53.005
Oh, sorry. Just saying random things.

13:53.089 --> 13:56.676
I don't know anything about Igarashi's
love life since we started high school.

13:56.759 --> 13:58.553
Maybe he's still single?

13:58.636 --> 14:01.138
- Maybe he's taken? Who knows.
- <i>Girlfriend?</i>

14:02.765 --> 14:03.766
<i>What?</i>

14:05.726 --> 14:07.645
- What a lovely meal.
- What a lovely meal.

14:07.728 --> 14:10.189
Yeah! Outta my way!

14:10.273 --> 14:11.274
Would you pipe down?

14:13.859 --> 14:17.947
- I'll be damned if anyone beats me!
- Oh, man. Someone's using it.

14:18.030 --> 14:19.532
- Get back here!
- Let's go elsewhere.

14:19.615 --> 14:20.741
MATSURI - ONDO NO MASTER

14:20.825 --> 14:21.993
There! There! There!

14:22.076 --> 14:23.077
Ouch!

14:23.160 --> 14:24.537
Sorry, Yota!

14:24.620 --> 14:25.621
UPPI PURI

14:25.705 --> 14:26.831
A photo while we're here!

14:26.914 --> 14:28.416
Am I even allowed in this thing?

14:28.499 --> 14:29.625
Why wouldn't you be?

14:29.709 --> 14:31.127
I get nervous.

14:31.627 --> 14:34.797
<i>Ready? Three, two, one...</i>

14:34.881 --> 14:35.882
Yay!

14:37.300 --> 14:40.553
Welp, that was so much fun.

14:40.636 --> 14:43.306
I love this guilty pleasure
of messing around before exams.

14:43.389 --> 14:44.765
I could get hooked.

14:44.849 --> 14:46.893
Please don't get addicted.

14:46.976 --> 14:48.811
We'll hit the books again tomorrow.

14:49.937 --> 14:51.814
Yota!

14:52.690 --> 14:53.816
See you!

14:54.400 --> 14:55.651
- See you.
- Bye-bye.

15:00.948 --> 15:02.950
WE ARE
ADORBS

15:03.743 --> 15:05.620
- Good for you.
- What? Don't know what you mean.

15:05.703 --> 15:06.704
GRINNING - PRICKLY

15:09.999 --> 15:13.711
<i>I guess all we can do is hope
that he gets on with his next girlfriend.</i>

15:14.295 --> 15:17.298
<i>Come on, man. Of course she's going
to have had past relationships.</i>

15:17.965 --> 15:21.802
<i>But honestly? With Igarashi?
It's just too out there.</i>

15:22.803 --> 15:29.226
<i>I kind of get how she'd have...
feelings for Yota, but...</i>

15:29.936 --> 15:31.896
<i>No. I don't want to "get" that.</i>

15:34.440 --> 15:35.441
BONK

15:35.524 --> 15:37.485
- Oh, man.
- Hey, what's up?

15:37.568 --> 15:40.237
<i>I don't get it at all.</i>

15:44.492 --> 15:46.494
Told you. 'Vators are the best.

15:46.577 --> 15:50.957
You Azumis are the only ones I know
who call elevators "'vators"...

15:59.715 --> 16:01.175
<i>Back in middle school,</i>

16:02.259 --> 16:04.512
<i>I hated Tsubasa Igarashi.</i>

16:05.096 --> 16:06.764
- Looks lame.
- <i>Our misaligned personalities.</i>

16:06.847 --> 16:09.016
- It's serious, man.
- <i>His unrequited love for me.</i>

16:10.351 --> 16:13.020
- Come, now. She's got Igarashi.
- <i>Everyone ignoring my feelings.</i>

16:13.104 --> 16:15.648
- Don't keep Igarashi waiting.
- <i>Everyone only wanting a good time.</i>

16:15.731 --> 16:18.275
<i>I hated everything. Everything.</i>

16:19.777 --> 16:23.447
<i>But that's not the reason
I want to avoid talking about him.</i>

16:24.824 --> 16:27.785
<i>It's because of what I did to him.</i>

16:30.413 --> 16:31.414
You.

16:34.625 --> 16:36.168
What's with the hair?

16:36.252 --> 16:37.253
WHOA

16:37.336 --> 16:38.838
M-Me?

16:38.921 --> 16:41.424
It was some wild color
the last time I saw you too.

16:41.507 --> 16:43.259
MATCH HIS VIBES FOR NOW
FIDGET FIDGET

16:43.342 --> 16:45.761
So, what?
I look good no matter what, am I right?

16:45.845 --> 16:47.179
Gosh, your fidgeting is gross.

16:47.805 --> 16:50.683
<i>He's acting like I'm not even here.</i>

16:52.476 --> 16:54.478
<i>I'm out of that fish tank,</i>

16:55.521 --> 16:59.275
<i>but the more I get to know myself,
the more I hate myself.</i>

17:02.611 --> 17:03.654
<i>I...</i>

17:04.155 --> 17:08.075
I never liked you. Not even for a second.

17:08.659 --> 17:13.581
<i>I've been too afraid
to face the one I hurt with my own malice.</i>

17:14.498 --> 17:15.916
<i>I'm nothing but a coward.</i>

17:18.169 --> 17:19.170
See you.

17:24.425 --> 17:25.426
Igarashi.

17:31.098 --> 17:32.099
What do you want?

17:33.976 --> 17:36.103
Are you enjoying high school?

17:38.105 --> 17:41.609
What? Are you
some long-lost relative, or something?

17:41.692 --> 17:42.735
GONG

17:42.818 --> 17:44.236
<i>Crap... What to do?</i>

17:44.320 --> 17:46.363
<i>That clapback was actually hilarious.</i>

17:47.073 --> 17:49.408
<i>I knew it. We can't converse.</i>

17:49.909 --> 17:51.035
I'm fine.

17:52.161 --> 17:54.955
And it's not like I need
your concern, either.

18:00.836 --> 18:04.423
You really surprised me there
when you stopped Igarashi like that.

18:04.507 --> 18:06.509
EPISODE: TALKING A BIT MORE
BEFORE WE GO HOME

18:06.592 --> 18:07.593
Thanks.

18:08.761 --> 18:09.929
I wonder why I did it?

18:10.012 --> 18:13.766
I had so much fun with you guys today,
eating dinner and stuff.

18:13.849 --> 18:15.059
Maybe that's why?

18:15.559 --> 18:17.103
I definitely acted out of character.

18:17.686 --> 18:18.771
Koyun.

18:26.362 --> 18:28.364
Here. Thanks for this.

18:28.447 --> 18:30.991
Excuse me? What's with the bag?

18:31.075 --> 18:35.871
Who cares? It's not like you're gonna see
anyone on your way home.

18:37.540 --> 18:40.126
<i>I did. And it was her, of all people...</i>

18:40.709 --> 18:42.878
Are you enjoying high school?

18:43.504 --> 18:45.047
You're one to talk.

18:47.633 --> 18:48.634
What a pain.

18:52.888 --> 18:53.889
Say...

18:54.473 --> 18:57.810
You only went out with Igarashi
because of me, right?

18:58.435 --> 19:02.857
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have spoken out
of turn without considering your feelings.

19:04.817 --> 19:05.818
What?

19:05.901 --> 19:07.319
What?

19:07.403 --> 19:09.905
You spoke out of turn?

19:09.989 --> 19:12.366
Yeah, didn't I?

19:12.449 --> 19:14.076
We were here once before, chatting,

19:14.160 --> 19:16.829
where I told you it's "good enough"
and you're being "greedy."

19:16.912 --> 19:19.748
You did? Maybe...

19:19.832 --> 19:22.042
What? That's it?

19:22.126 --> 19:24.211
Sorry, my memory's a bit hazy.

19:24.295 --> 19:25.296
CONFUSED

19:25.379 --> 19:28.299
What? Then why did you two date?

19:31.552 --> 19:32.887
- It's a secret.
- What?

19:32.970 --> 19:33.971
SHOCK

19:34.597 --> 19:38.559
If I tell you,
you're gonna look down on me.

19:38.642 --> 19:39.727
Hey, hold up...

19:41.478 --> 19:43.647
That comment is not allowed to slide.

19:43.731 --> 19:44.732
Such force...

19:46.775 --> 19:47.818
I...

19:48.944 --> 19:52.698
I thought I'd feel better
if I fell in love with somebody

19:52.781 --> 19:54.241
who actually loves me.

19:55.492 --> 19:58.495
But I didn't feel better.
In fact, it only made things worse.

19:59.538 --> 20:01.665
And in the end,
I only wound up hurting Igarashi.

20:02.875 --> 20:05.211
<i>Or rather,
I went out of my way to hurt him.</i>

20:06.545 --> 20:08.714
I was acting in a way
that went against my heart.

20:08.797 --> 20:10.966
All I could think about was myself.

20:11.842 --> 20:15.262
And, Miki... You hate people who do that.

20:17.514 --> 20:19.016
I have nothing to say to that.

20:19.600 --> 20:24.605
I mean, no matter what you did,
Igarashi was going to get hurt, right?

20:24.688 --> 20:27.274
And that's not your fault, or anything.

20:27.858 --> 20:32.905
And besides. I wouldn't know
how to hate you even if I tried.

20:32.988 --> 20:35.241
And I'd never hate you
over something like that.

20:35.324 --> 20:36.325
BASHFUL

20:36.408 --> 20:37.409
OH?

20:37.493 --> 20:38.994
All right!

20:39.078 --> 20:42.122
Let's overwrite these sucky memories
with new, happy relationships.

20:42.206 --> 20:44.375
No, thank you.

20:44.458 --> 20:46.126
You can do that for the both of us.

20:46.210 --> 20:48.796
- Who would be good for you?
- What?

20:48.879 --> 20:49.922
(IGNORING)
WHAT SORT OF PERSON...

20:50.506 --> 20:53.175
I'd like someone who's
the complete opposite to Igarashi for you.

20:53.259 --> 20:55.427
Someone kind, with his head in the clouds.

20:55.511 --> 20:58.430
Someone who can meet you at your pace.

20:59.014 --> 21:03.060
I'd like someone who likes you for you.

21:03.143 --> 21:06.188
Someone kind, and with a big heart.

21:07.398 --> 21:09.650
- No, don't bother about me.
- No, don't bother about me.

21:09.733 --> 21:11.694
JINX

21:14.780 --> 21:17.908
Well, it's not like dating is
the be-all and end-all.

21:17.992 --> 21:20.035
I'm having plenty of fun
just as we are now.

21:20.119 --> 21:23.664
But a little love could be
just the cherry on top, right?

21:23.747 --> 21:25.791
Like a cherry tomato in your bento.

21:27.418 --> 21:29.211
Is that the right saying?

21:29.295 --> 21:30.671
Who even knows.

21:31.547 --> 21:32.756
<i>Love.</i>

21:32.840 --> 21:36.677
Koyuki, do you like Igarashi?

21:38.345 --> 21:39.596
No, I don't.

21:40.097 --> 21:41.890
That's just what people are saying.

21:42.599 --> 21:43.684
I see...

21:46.020 --> 21:47.271
You know what?

21:47.354 --> 21:50.357
Atagawa's been really
coming on strong with me lately.

21:51.525 --> 21:54.737
I'm not interested in anyone
other than the person I like.

21:54.820 --> 21:56.822
Honestly, it's getting annoying.

22:04.580 --> 22:05.831
<i>Hey, Miki.</i>

22:06.540 --> 22:09.626
<i>My heart isn't as pure as yours.</i>

22:09.710 --> 22:11.795
- See you.
- I'll await your tomato report.

22:11.879 --> 22:13.589
<i>Personally...</i>

22:13.672 --> 22:14.882
Tomato report! I love it.

22:14.965 --> 22:16.675
<i>I could never recommend myself to anyone.</i>

22:18.344 --> 22:19.511
<i>So...</i>

22:22.848 --> 22:24.850
<i>You find happiness, Miki.</i>

23:50.352 --> 23:55.357
Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
